==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Decent damage.
* No endlag when using moves.
* No dash on melee attacks, making it great to farm with [[Elemental]] fruits.
* Low mastery requirements.

|'''[Z] Assassinate'''
* Decent damage.

|'''[X] Raging Wind'''
* Quick start.
* Good range and [[AoE]].
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* No stun whatsoever.
* Performs terribly in air combat.
* Pretty expensive for players in the [[First Sea]].
* Generally bad in later seas, so it is recommended to replace this in the [[Second Sea]].

|'''[Z] Assassinate'''
* Short range.

|'''[X] Raging Wind'''
* Low stun.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* In the moveset, the Dual-Headed Blade is called "Headed Blade" (due to the lack of wording space).
* {{Ability|X}} appears to be an upgraded version of the [[Wardens Sword]]'s {{Ability|Wardens Sword|X}}.
* The Dual-Headed Blade is the third most expensive sword in the [[First Sea]] behind [[Soul Cane]] and [[Bisento]].

